From 2a42d674d273fe4dbf5693d3c3f42ccd74767033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iitimii <timiiowolabi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:24:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/24] S1a-pre: add missing cstdarg include for GCC builds

tools/duo/duo.cpp uses va_list/va_start/va_end in jtrace() without
including <cstdarg>. AppleClang pulls the declarations in
transitively through another header; GCC does not, so the Linux
container build of llama-duo fails. Add the include explicitly.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
---
 tools/duo/duo.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/duo/duo.cpp b/tools/duo/duo.cpp
index 0e7fdbd..28d4503 100644
--- a/tools/duo/duo.cpp
+++ b/tools/duo/duo.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "sampling.h"
 
 #include <cinttypes>
+#include <cstdarg>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstring>
-- 
